: \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"ab1a39264e4df0631a705309f94b79fd3ef0ef62703fe5aa797c104eb25a7dd8","event_uuid":"37b1a50d-b0af-4c22-b330-3dc48702008b","position":{"commit_sha":"8256432d4d1098f501ad7fb6498076100ab91863","position":"1788514429295932657-37b1a50d-b0af-4c22-b330-3dc48702008b"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"cae5a5f348527e958299ab990907053e044ad3ceba74bc2e37d16ade85170d2d","event_uuid":"c3fbe88d-8c8b-4ea9-b1a7-fbdfcd30c723","position":{"commit_sha":"71c7615b2a80d06669cd7e7113eefa5f358694a7","position":"1788515597084314711-c3fbe88d-8c8b-4ea9-b1a7-fbdfcd30c723"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"32bb9b07bc4926b161203360ae4eb84c71541c52ea107d8eafdeff78378e1019","event_uuid":"4549e11b-f065-49ba-95ff-9daec903f3bc","position":{"commit_sha":"13affbb4a21c53479d2844148557152c6e224fc9","position":"1788516858032943739-4549e11b-f065-49ba-95ff-9daec903f3bc"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788318528120277269,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"7546f5f5-6d81-48b0-b122-d4f2f6e14665","relation":"blocks","target_id":"a5bf-c1f8-3950-4f87"},{"link_uuid":"0c0d5b13-f058-40d9-944a-4b90f37bfd7c","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"10fb-ff5e-d3b8-4233"},{"link_uuid":"de3cb769-0958-433b-98aa-e88d0fdd668e","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"b744-f5d1-b6b3-4904"},{"link_uuid":"04db8769-bd09-4273-b9e6-5a78c0a275f0","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"0648-251b-bd53-40de"},{"link_uuid":"3f1769ef-3e0a-45e7-b711-56c7d6316db5","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"5c23-f673-90df-411b"},{"link_uuid":"37b1a50d-b0af-4c22-b330-3dc48702008b","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"ca48-2904-7cad-4752"},{"link_uuid":"c3fbe88d-8c8b-4ea9-b1a7-fbdfcd30c723","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"f83a-fa72-9abb-4c48"},{"link_uuid":"4549e11b-f065-49ba-95ff-9daec903f3bc","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"7bc5-4ed6-6559-49b3"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe sibling admission runner fills fixture coverage once. Two things reopen gaps: a criterion\nadded to the registry later starts with no fixture, and a criterion whose candidates all failed\nto reproduce is left with none. Coverage then decays until someone notices. A repair loop that\nspends money unattended needs a bound independent of anyone watching it.\n\n## Approach\n\n**Gap-only scope.** Each run considers only criteria that\n`criteria.effective_routing('.', gate_key='plan_review')` reports and for which no spec file\nexists under `.rebar/evals/` or `src/rebar/llm/eval_specs/`. Criteria that already have a\nfixture are never revisited, so the loop's work shrinks monotonically to zero — unattended spend\nbounded by construction, not by a watchdog.\n\n**Quarantine breaker (a persistent ticket-based quarantine, not an in-memory breaker;** the\nsibling a5bf records the pattern). Two triggers file a quarantine ticket titled exactly\n`unreliable-criterion: <criterion-id>` — the literal prefix `unreliable-criterion: ` (WITH the\ntrailing space) then the registry criterion id:\n\n1. **Three consecutive failed runs.** The loop persists, per criterion, a consecutive-failure\n   counter in its rebar state file (beside the due-stamp). A run fails for a criterion on either\n   of two signals, each read from a named sub-step's report: the admission runner's per-criterion\n   reproduction-failure result, or the emitter's `FixtureEmitReport.skipped_unbalanced` (no case\n   on both sides of the fire/no-fire axis). On the third consecutive such run the loop files the\n   ticket. The counter RESETS to zero when the criterion becomes covered or its ticket closes.\n2. **Runner-declared un-minable (first-encounter).** The admission runner itself decides a\n   criterion cannot be inline-admitted and records a skip-drift entry (`observed=\"skipped\"`)\n   with one of its two DISTINCT reasons: `not-inline-admissible` (the ISF class,\n   `eval_solver.INLINE_UNADMISSIBLE_CRITERIA = frozenset({'ISF'})`) or\n   `container-material-unrecoverable` (the container criteria `CONTAINER_CRITERIA` =\n   G3/G4/decomp-shape). These are two reasons, NOT one \"not inline-runnable\" class — the loop\n   does not re-derive inline-runnability; it CONSUMES the runner's verdict. On the first run\n   whose drift report carries such an entry for a criterion, it files the ticket immediately, so\n   no spend is wasted mining a criterion the runner will not admit.\n\n**How the quarantine feeds the selector — the loop OWNS this wiring; it is NEW work.**\n`fixture_selection.select_candidates` does NOT read ticket titles: it skips only criteria in a\ncaller-supplied `unreliable: dict[criterion_id -> ticket_id]` map (its internal reason string\n`unreliable-criterion:{ticket_id}` is keyed on ticket id, a DIFFERENT string from the title).\nThis loop builds that map: it queries OPEN tickets whose title matches `unreliable-criterion:\n<id>`, parses the criterion id, and passes `{id: ticket_id}` to the selector. Creation is\nIDEMPOTENT — filed only when no OPEN ticket with that exact title exists — and the map builder\ndedupes by criterion id (lowest ticket id wins), so a rare concurrent double-create is\nself-healing: the selector still skips the criterion and the extra ticket is a closeable\nduplicate. The once-per-interval due-stamp serializes runs.\n\n**Portability.** Recurring work must not depend on a CI provider. The trigger is\noperation-linked with an in-process due-stamp: the loop records its last run in the repository's\nrebar state, and a rebar plan-review operation advances it once the configured interval\n(default 30 days) has elapsed. It is also directly invocable as a command, so an operator, a\ncron, or any CI provider can drive it — no step depends on a POSIX-only shell.\n\n**Unattended spend bound + failure disposition.** Mining is free; only admission costs. Each\nrun pre-flights through `ledger.reserve(..., cap_usd=25.0)` against the loop's own ledger and\nstops when remaining headroom cannot cover the next criterion, leaving the rest for the next\ninterval — bounding unattended spend to $25 per interval however many gaps exist. Because\n`finalize()` prices ACTUAL usage, a subsequent `reserve` re-checks cumulative actual spend, so\nan actual that overran its estimate makes the NEXT `reserve` raise `BudgetExceeded` (FATAL,\nnon-retryable): the run stops with already-finalized criteria admitted and their spend\nreconciled, and the next interval resumes. A criterion whose candidates fail to reproduce is not\nan error — it increments the breaker counter (trigger #1) and the run continues.\n\n## Scope\n\nThe loop command, its due-stamp trigger and interval configuration, the per-criterion\nconsecutive-failure counter, the open-ticket title→`unreliable` map builder that feeds the\nselector, both quarantine triggers, the idempotent `unreliable-criterion:` ticket creation, and\nthe loop's own ledger file. It reuses the sibling selector, emitter and admission runner.\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- Repairing a criterion recorded as unreliable; that is the work the filed ticket represents.\n- Revisiting or rewriting a criterion that already has a fixture.\n- Any human curation step between mining and admission.\n\n## Compatibility and rollback\n\nAdditive: a new command, a new state stamp/counter, and a new ledger file. No existing command,\nspec, or persisted format changes. Back-out is deleting the command and its state; nothing reads\nit if the command is absent.\n\n## Testing\n\nUnit tests (each named in an AC below) run against a stubbed admission runner over a temporary\nstore, deterministic without a model; a subprocess test covers the command with no CI\nenvironment.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] A criterion that already has a spec file is absent from a run's attempt list; `pytest`\n      asserts the selected id set excludes it (gap-only scope).\n- [ ] The third consecutive failed run creates exactly one ticket titled\n      `unreliable-criterion: <criterion-id>`, and the first and second do not; `pytest` against\n      a temporary store asserts the title and the ticket count after each run.\n- [ ] A `skipped-unbalanced` run (from the emitter) increments the same counter as a runner\n      reproduction failure; `pytest` asserts the ticket appears after three mixed-kind runs.\n- [ ] A criterion with an open ticket of that title is absent from the attempt list; `pytest`\n      asserts the id is not selected (the loop's title→`unreliable`-map builder queries the open\n      ticket and passes it to `select_candidates`).\n- [ ] A criterion the runner declares un-minable — a container criterion (drift reason\n      `container-material-unrecoverable`) or an ISF-class one (`not-inline-admissible`) — is\n      quarantined on FIRST encounter: one ticket filed without three runs; `pytest` asserts the\n      ticket exists after a single run over each such seeded criterion.\n- [ ] Ticket creation is idempotent — a second run while the ticket is open creates no\n      duplicate; `pytest` asserts the ticket count stays 1 after a re-run.\n- [ ] A run stops before a criterion whose estimate exceeds remaining headroom and admits the\n      criteria it completed; `pytest` against the real `ledger.reserve` with `cap_usd=25.0`\n      asserts the admitted set and that the ledger total is at most 25.0.\n- [ ] The command runs with no CI environment variables set and reports its attempt list; a\n      `pytest` subprocess test with a cleared environment asserts this.\n- [ ] The due-stamp advances only after the configured interval; `pytest` asserts no attempt at\n      interval minus one day and one at the interval.\n\n## Definition of Done\n\n`make lint`, `make typecheck` and `make test` pass; a seeded three-failure history produces the\nticket and the selector skip.\n\n## Budget\n\n**Hard cap $100** for building this child and its first runs. Each unattended run is separately\ncapped at $25 by its own pre-flight; total cost falls to zero once every criterion is covered or\nrecorded as unreliable.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/llm/evals/fixture_mining/heal.py","reason":"The gap-only loop: attempt selection, the per-criterion consecutive-failure counter and its state file, the open-ticket title->unreliable map builder that feeds the selector, both quarantine triggers (three consecutive failures AND not-inline-runnable container/ISF), idempotent unreliable-criterion ticket creation, and the per-run ledger budget stop."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_llm_eval_commands.py","reason":"Expose the loop as a directly invocable command handler so an operator, a cron or any CI provider can drive it."},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_parsers/advanced/llm_eval.py","reason":"Register the loop command's argparse subparser and its interval/options flags."},{"path":"src/rebar/_config_schema.py","reason":"Add the loop's interval setting, defaulting to 30 days."},{"path":"tests/unit/test_fixture_heal.py","reason":"Unit tests for gap-only selection, the three-strike breaker and its exact ticket title, the container/ISF immediate quarantine, idempotent creation, the skip on an open ticket, the per-run ledger stop and the due-stamp interval."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["blocks","a5bf-c1f8-3950-4f87"],["parent","65dd-e93b-666a-4caa"],["relates_to","0648-251b-bd53-40de"],["relates_to","10fb-ff5e-d3b8-4233"],["relates_to","5c23-f673-90df-411b"],["relates_to","7bc5-4ed6-6559-49b3"],["relates_to","b744-f5d1-b6b3-4904"],["relates_to","ca48-2904-7cad-4752"],["relates_to","f83a-fa72-9abb-4c48"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"65dd-e93b-666a-4caa","parent_status_uuid":"789da82c-3080-4847-9cb6-2bdfb0940bfa","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["plan-review","evals","fixtures","budget"],"ticket_id":"1cef-7fbc-e402-467c","ticket_type":"story","title":"Gap-only self-healing fixture loop with an unreliable-criterion circuit breaker","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["9105d9c0-293e-4068-94bc-b60056eedfef","143e66a0-2106-470f-b507-4e29650ecc9b","05f32f76-baee-4194-8333-73fb1404c342","65d535c1-8c81-4e69-8009-a571761b93fe","789da82c-3080-4847-9cb6-2bdfb0940bfa","7628d769-ab0a-46fe-bd79-4a1c677cf123","0c0d5b13-f058-40d9-944a-4b90f37bfd7c","de3cb769-0958-433b-98aa-e88d0fdd668e","04db8769-bd09-4273-b9e6-5a78c0a275f0","3f1769ef-3e0a-45e7-b711-56c7d6316db5","37b1a50d-b0af-4c22-b330-3dc48702008b","c3fbe88d-8c8b-4ea9-b1a7-fbdfcd30c723","4549e11b-f065-49ba-95ff-9daec903f3bc"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788520820855156001,"uuid":"a5ccb7df-e155-4980